    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0032" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.34/255: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-17T20:00:00-04:00">February 17,
                            1942—8 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Your 100, February 9, noon. The Navy Department states that it sees no
                    objection to the transfer to the Chinese Government of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tutuila</hi> together with its equipment and stores. The
                    Navy Department is initiating action to carry out the transfer under <pb
                        facs="0033" n="23" xml:id="pg23"/> the provisions of “Defense Aid”. It is
                    understood that, without obtaining additional specific legislative authority,
                    there is no other available method of effecting the transfer.</p>
                <p>The Chinese Embassy is being informed of the foregoing, with the request that the
                    matter be considered as confidential until the transfer has been actually
                    effected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
